finding: P2 src/standard/physics/runtime.ts:1874-1881: The public step contract says only to disable automatic stepping to own solve ordering. It does not say that Character's characters system and other producers ordered before StepPhysicsSystem are not ordered before the caller. A fixed caller can run before the character sweep despite using the automatic-step anchor; pending-authoring sync does not run that producer. State at stepPhysics/enableAutomaticStep where a game acts that it must order its calling system after the character sweep and other before-solve producers (and that the automatic step remains additional unless disabled). P2 src/standard/physics/runtime.ts:1914 (phaseNames at 2449): Manual solves still emit phases under StandardPhysics/step/*, although their enclosing scheduler measurement is the game's calling system. With automatic stepping disabled, StandardPhysics/step measures only the no-solve pose-sync callback while its children contain all manual solves. The profiler thus presents solve phases as parts of a parent that did not perform them (and can be shorter than its children). Attribute manual phase samples to the executing caller, preserving the automatic path's hierarchy, and cover zero/multiple calls with a record sink. Current step tests do not exercise this.
